Fixed. Evidence file: /home/skynet/1-agent/docs/evidence/phase4-fast-2026-11-23/workspaces/fast/run-1/bug-fix-last-index/counter.rs

Before:
pub fn last_index(len: usize) -> usize {
    len
}

After:
pub fn last_index(len: usize) -> usize {
    len.saturating_sub(1)
}

Exact change: the single return expression `len` was replaced with `len.saturating_sub(1)` (1 line added, 1 removed). For a non-empty slice (`len >= 1`) this yields the last valid index `len - 1`; for `len == 0` it saturates to 0 instead of underflowing, so no panic in debug builds. File is now 69 bytes, written atomically and re-read to confirm contents; sha256 c7c78b8ac7d84bc3dcd2781e56f6bfee81cbbf59af2ae7d16c186605fb5dd297 (previous f83d876da95472a013aac778d27c8130590739cc84d5a56046c078d26b4a2628).
